### Create a draft Coagulant formula (v1)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/formulas
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "chemicalType": "COAGULANT",
  "baseDose": 2.0,
  "minDose": 0.5,
  "maxDose": 10.0,
  "createdBy": "wes",
  "notes": "Initial coagulant curve",
  "inputs": [
    { "readingTag": "QC1_Turbidity", "coefficient": 0.15 },
    { "readingTag": "InfluentFlowRate", "coefficient": 0.02 }
  ]
}

### List all formulas
GET http://localhost:8080/api/formulas

### Get one formula by id (replace 1 with the id returned above)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/formulas/1

### Approve it (replace 1 with the id)
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/formulas/1/approve
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "approvedBy": "wes"
}

### Activate it (replace 1 with the id)
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/formulas/1/activate

### Fetch the active formula for a chemical type -- this is what Ignition will call
GET http://localhost:8080/api/formulas/active/COAGULANT

### Try activating a DRAFT directly -- should fail with 409 Conflict
# (create a second draft first, then try to activate it without approving)

### Push a process reading (simulating Ignition)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/readings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tagName": "QC1_Turbidity",
  "value": 3.42
}

### List readings
GET http://localhost:8080/api/readings

### Push an alarm event (simulating Ignition)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/alarms
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "alarmName": "Chlorine Breakthrough",
  "priority": "High",
  "state": "Active",
  "sourcePath": "WaterQuality/QC2_ChlorineResidual"
}

### List alarms
GET http://localhost:8080/api/alarms

### ============================================================
### Placeholder formulas for the remaining 4 pumps -- arbitrary
### demo coefficients (same spirit as the Coagulant one), just
### enough to exercise the full 5-pump calc loop end to end.
### Adjust readingTag/coefficient values however you'd like.
### Run each POST, note the id it returns, then approve + activate
### it the same way you did for Coagulant.
### ============================================================

### SH formula (baseline InfluentFlowRate, trim QC2_ChlorineResidual)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/formulas
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "chemicalType": "SH",
  "baseDose": 1.5,
  "minDose": 0.3,
  "maxDose": 8.0,
  "createdBy": "wes",
  "notes": "Placeholder SH curve",
  "inputs": [
    { "readingTag": "InfluentFlowRate", "coefficient": 0.01 },
    { "readingTag": "QC2_ChlorineResidual", "coefficient": 0.5 }
  ]
}

### SBS formula (baseline FiltrateFlowRate, trim QC2_ChlorineResidual)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/formulas
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "chemicalType": "SBS",
  "baseDose": 1.0,
  "minDose": 0.2,
  "maxDose": 6.0,
  "createdBy": "wes",
  "notes": "Placeholder SBS curve",
  "inputs": [
    { "readingTag": "FiltrateFlowRate", "coefficient": 0.01 },
    { "readingTag": "QC2_ChlorineResidual", "coefficient": 1.2 }
  ]
}

### Antiscalant formula (Hardness, InfluentFlowRate, InfluentTemperature)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/formulas
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "chemicalType": "ANTISCALANT",
  "baseDose": 0.8,
  "minDose": 0.2,
  "maxDose": 5.0,
  "createdBy": "wes",
  "notes": "Placeholder Antiscalant curve",
  "inputs": [
    { "readingTag": "Hardness", "coefficient": 0.02 },
    { "readingTag": "InfluentFlowRate", "coefficient": 0.005 },
    { "readingTag": "InfluentTemperature", "coefficient": 0.01 }
  ]
}

### Caustic formula (baseline ROFeedFlowRate, trim ROFeed_pH)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/formulas
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "chemicalType": "CAUSTIC",
  "baseDose": 1.2,
  "minDose": 0.3,
  "maxDose": 7.0,
  "createdBy": "wes",
  "notes": "Placeholder Caustic curve",
  "inputs": [
    { "readingTag": "ROFeedFlowRate", "coefficient": 0.008 },
    { "readingTag": "ROFeed_pH", "coefficient": -0.3 }
  ]
}

### Then for each new formula id (use the ids returned above):
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/formulas/5/approve
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "approvedBy": "wes"
}

###
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/formulas/5/activate

### Once all 5 are ACTIVE, confirm with:
GET http://localhost:8080/api/formulas
